## goal
Implement `spec-engine` only: local catalog contract, `spec.json` contract, catalog validation, eligibility filters (`kind` / `installation_type` / `voltage` / `frequency_hz`), `auto-select-model` using `closest-airflow-above`, strict fail when no eligible model satisfies demand, `lower-power` tie-break, `top-3-valid` alternatives, and end-to-end integration from `proyectos/1/input.json` + `proyectos/1/resultados.json` to `proyectos/1/spec.json`.

## assumptions
- Source of truth = `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-23-spec-engine-design.md`.
- No `pdd/spec-engine/explore` or `pdd/spec-engine/requirements` artifacts exist yet; plan grounded on spec + repo evidence.
- Existing project fixture is canonical: `input.json` provides `equipment.id/alias/kind` and `resultados.json` provides `equipment_results[].required_m3_h_assigned`.
- `proyectos/1/input.json` currently has `installation_type`, `voltage`, and `frequency_hz` as `null` for `E1`; v1 must treat null as “no filter applied”, not mismatch.
- v1 alternatives convention should be frozen to **exclude selected model** and list next best valid candidates only, matching spec recommendation.
- Repo pattern should mirror `lib/calc-engine`: pure selection logic + thin runner/integration layer.

## constraints
- Exclude web search, internet fallback, vendor availability, pricing, multi-unit optimization, and memory generation.
- Exclude under-sized substitutions: if no eligible model has `airflow_m3_h >= required_m3_h`, selection must fail.
- Keep sourcing policy fixed to `local-only` and selection mode fixed to `auto-select-model`.
- Keep tie-break fixed to `lower-power`; do not add secondary commercial heuristics.
- Keep output focused on single-project artifact generation under `/proyectos/[id]/spec.json`.
- Do not redesign upstream `input.json` or `resultados.json` contracts.

